  "reviewedReason": "added blackbox exclusion scope to drift-detector, hard/soft failure asymmetry and tolerateInvalidConfig to loader",
  "aspectResults": {
    "deterministic": {
      "satisfied": true,
      "reason": "The drift-detector.ts uses only deterministic operations: SHA-256 hashing via hashTrackedFiles (line 98, 215), filesystem reads to verify graph-declared paths exist (allPathsMissing at line 177, access calls), and graph state traversal. No Math.random, Date.now, network calls, or implicit system state in core logic. Filesystem reads (access at line 181, hashTrackedFiles) fall under exception (3) — verifying graph-declared mapping paths exist on disk, deterministic relative to filesystem state. The mtime optimization (lines 95-97, 212-214) passes stored data as input to hashTrackedFiles rather than reading system time in core logic. All categorization and status determination (lines 132-145) is pure logic over computed values."
    },
    "posix-paths": {
      "satisfied": true,
      "reason": "All path handling in drift-detector.ts applies the POSIX normalization pattern (.trim().replace(/\\\\/g, '/').replace(/\\/+$/, '')) before any comparison or storage. Specifically: filterNodePath at line 49, file paths at line 111, categorizeFile inputs at lines 172-173, absPath construction at line 179, normalizedNodePath at line 202, and yggPrefix at line 224. The file also delegates to normalizeMappingPaths (line 59) for mapping paths, which handles normalization upstream. No raw path comparisons occur without prior normalization."
    }
  },
